## Separate-face boundary components

On Audit.134, keep one recipient vertex per exceptional face instead of
merging all inner terminals. The same physical midpoint bound and
atomic marked-measure proof show only that boundary-reaching components
number o(D). Interior-only components can be linear and are retained
in the incidence ledger.

Let f_boundary be the number of exceptional faces in boundary-reaching
components and N_interior the number of non-atomic trains in the other
components. Exact graph incidence gives

    3*f_boundary >= f+2*k-2*c_boundary
    3*(atomic_train_count+N_interior) <= 5*(f-k+c_boundary).

Consequently the candidate chain is

    c_boundary=o(D), atomic mass >= 2*s_2
      -> (f-k)/D >= (6/5)*s_2-o(1)
      -> [2(q-k)-k-z]/D >= pi+(6/5)*s_2-o(1)
      -> (q-k)/D >= pi/2+(3/5)*s_2-o(1)
      -> the whole positive one-cell collar range is empty.

The new constant is 2.1421840109, strictly above 2*pi/3.
The exact verifier checks another 354 separate-face graphs and 886
component cancellations. It does not certify the analytic limiting
argument or source optimality.

The Audit.52 canonical full-core depletion floor applies to
mu=(q-k+m)/D-o(1). Despite sharing FC3's numerical constant, it
does not imply a floor on t=(q-k)/D when m is linear. This live
comparison corrects the stale unpromoted-status note for that theorem.

Classification: proved candidate awaiting independent audit/promotion,
registry unreviewed and canonical=false. High-t Type II and the
macroscopic-container branch remain open. The next obligation is a
global geometric or motion argument; linear face count alone is
compatible with the available boundary-order area budget.

